1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Turun tuomiokirkkoseurakunnan arkisto > Ruotsalaisen seurakunnan rippikirja, I, I (1856-1865): Tiedosto 93 https://astia.narc.fi/uusiastia/viewer/?fileId=5890639151&aineistoId=1270035304
2 CONT
2 CONT Keuruu rippikirja 1910-1919 (AP_IV I Aa:21)  Sivu 1358 Suolahti No 9, Kantola tp; (Heikinheimo, Kepplerus, Råbergh, Procopé, Aarnio, Mykkänen, Aro) ; SSHY http://www.sukuhistoria.fi/sshy/sivut/jasenille/paikat.php?bid=44202&pnum=7
2 CONC 3 / Viitattu 03.12.2023
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1838, a woman climbed Mont Blanc with 18 bottles of wine, 26 roast chickens and a carrier pigeon. Why are we only hearing about this now?! ⁠
2 CONT ⁠
2 CONT The person in question was Henriette D’Angeville, who became the first woman to complete the ascent unaided. Her outfit, homemade as there were no climbing clothes for women at the time, included a controversial pair of knickerboc
2 CONC kers, a corset to cover them up and a very fetching bonnet. ⁠
2 CONT ⁠
2 CONT The reason we’re only hearing about this now is because this summer adventurer, writer and presenter Lise Wortley (aka Woman with Altitude) is going to recreate the climb. Probably minus the wine, but in the same brilliant outfit.
2 CONC  It’s part of her ongoing mission to highlight female explorers and pioneers who’ve been left out of the history books, and to inspire more women to take to the outdoors. We’ll be working with her on her training walks in six of t
2 CONC he UK’s national parks and helping her raise awareness of her mission.   ⁠
2 CONT ⁠
2 CONT When Henriette D’Angeville reached the summit of Mont Blanc, she had her guides lift her into the air so that she could “go higher than any man has before.” With Lise’s help, she’s going to keep soaring.
2 CONT
2 CONT READ ALSO: https://www.droidalerts.com/separated-for-what-felt-like-forever-a-german-shepherd-collapsed-into-his-owners-arms-with-a-whimper-of-pure-joy/
